    "subject": "UAE open finance: why 12 of 30 registrations publish an auth server",
    "description": "",
    "publish_date": "2026-10-29T09:09:36.055178Z",
    "body": "<!-- buttondown-editor-mode: fancy --><table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td style=\"padding:0;border-top:2px solid #E8A85C;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><div style=\"height:12px;line-height:12px;font-size:0;\">&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"Open Finance OS weekly briefing, issue 1\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/d8343b7a-3a46-49e8-a3aa-164e05ff9efb.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\">Hello, and welcome to the first issue of the Open Finance OS weekly briefing.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\">Each week we'll pull together what's happening in UAE open finance, plus a few things from further afield worth knowing about. It's a community project, so if something's useful (or missing), hit reply and tell us.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:28px 0 14px 0;padding:0 0 0 10px;border-left:4px solid #E8A85C;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#0D4F4F;font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;\">This week in UAE open finance</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"Bar chart of this issue's 7 stories by topic: UAE ecosystem 3, agentic payments 2, Pay by Bank in Europe 1, commercial models 1\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/69f9d977-f05e-4ffc-8eef-9eb939404193.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"12 of 30 UAE registrations publish an authorization server\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/696a561d-ad0b-49d3-92fc-b1b9ab99ed95.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://openfinance-os.org/news/2026-10-29-12-of-30-uae-open-finance-authorization-servers/\">12 of 30: Why most UAE open finance registrations don't publish an authorization server</a></strong><br />\nOnly 12 of 30 production directory registrations publish an active authorization server, but that isn't a sign that 60% of the ecosystem is broken. In the UAE's centralised model, the Nebras-operated API Hub acts as the authorization server and consent store, and TPPs never call banks directly.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"1.42 million cumulative API calls, November 2025 to September 2026\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/81fb0abe-95a4-4b58-a1af-ccfb6cf86def.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://openfinance-os.org/news/2026-10-26-weekly-digest/\">This week in UAE Open Finance: 19 to 26 October</a></strong><br />\nThree registry changes: Zurich joined the production registry as an LFI, and EIB joined and added an LFI role. Al Tareq platform logs show 1,416,887 cumulative API calls from November 2025 to September 2026, with a 95.3% payment success rate.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"NBF Direct adds open finance with multi-bank access\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/2660481b-c36b-4dc6-a5c7-c9c064cb21d0.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://openfinance-os.org/news/2026-10-22-open-finance-arrives-on-the-nbf-direct-app-with-mu/\">Open finance arrives on the NBF Direct app with multi-bank access</a></strong><br />\nNational Bank of Fujairah began rolling out open finance in its NBF Direct app in September 2026, letting customers share their account data and do more in the app themselves.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"Sibos 2026: commercial models to scale A2A payments and AI services\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/f3faf407-d4a4-4627-bf3e-964074386596.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://openfinance-os.org/news/2026-10-27-why-open-banking-needs-sustainable-commercial-mode/\">Why open banking needs a sustainable commercial model to scale payments and AI services</a></strong><br />\nAt Sibos 2026, NatWest's Simon Eacott made the case that commercial models, A2A payments and AI are what take open banking to the next level. A useful lens for the UAE as usage grows.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"Pay by Bank via Mastercard Open Finance in 9 European markets\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/af89ae15-def1-49ef-9ddc-84c20c7d7b57.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://openfinance-os.org/news/2026-10-28-zencom-and-mastercard-expand-pay-by-bank-for-merch/\">Zen.com and Mastercard expand Pay by Bank across Europe</a></strong><br />\nZen.com now supports Pay by Bank through Mastercard Open Finance for merchant payments and wallet top-ups across nine European markets.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:28px 0 14px 0;padding:0 0 0 10px;border-left:4px solid #E8A85C;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#0D4F4F;font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;\">Agents and open finance</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\">How would an AI agent actually reach your bank account in the UAE? Here's the simplified path: the customer consents, a licensed TPP (or the agent it runs) makes the request, and the Nebras API Hub sits between it and the bank.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;\"><img alt=\"Diagram: customer consent flows to a TPP or AI agent, then the Nebras API Hub, then the LFI or bank; responses return the same way. AlTareq is the customer-facing brand and Aani the instant payment rail.\" src=\"https://assets.buttondown.email/images/eafd69a9-83b8-4c21-a185-35cba8175d17.png\" width=\"100%\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:0;\" /></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://corporate.visa.com/en/sites/visa-perspectives/newsroom/visa-bill-billtrust-launch-pilot.html\">Visa, BILL and Billtrust launch a live pilot for AI agent payments</a></strong> (Visa, 20 October)<br />\nAI agents registered through Visa's Trusted Agent Protocol are now paying approved supplier invoices end to end, using tokenised credentials instead of shared portal logins. It's an early real-world test of how an agent proves who it is and what it's allowed to do.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;\"><a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://www.mastercard.com/global/en/news-and-trends/press/2026/october/Mastercard-Agent-Pay-for-Machines-in-action.html\">Mastercard opens Agent Pay for Machines to developers</a></strong> (Mastercard, October)<br />\nBusinesses give an agent a spending limit, and the agent pays for services with signed vouchers that providers verify now and settle later. Early access APIs and a sandbox are open; no general availability date yet.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:28px 0 14px 0;padding:0 0 0 10px;border-left:4px solid #E8A85C;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#0D4F4F;font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;\">That's it for this week</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\">Thanks for reading the first issue. If you have news, data or a correction, just reply to this email. And if a colleague would find this useful, please forward it or point them to <a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://openfinance-os.org/newsletter\">openfinance-os.org/newsletter</a>.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\">Want to talk it through? <a style=\"color:#0D4F4F;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #E8A85C;\" href=\"https://join.slack.com/t/openfinance-os/shared_invite/zt-4f6yrsi0w-qPd32ve~7Czekf0BWJRgLQ\">Join the Open Finance OS community on Slack</a>, where we'll share each issue and start a discussion every week.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#132C2B;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;\">See you next week,<br />\nMichael</p>\n</td></tr></table>",
